{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"role":"article","title":"Getting Started with Gnusto","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"text":"Build and run your first text adventure, one piece at a time.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide walks you from an empty package to a small, playable game. By the end you will have declared two rooms and an object, wired them together, added a rule, tested a play session, and run the whole thing at a prompt. It assumes you can write basic Swift; it assumes nothing about interactive fiction."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Prefer to start from something that already runs? The repo ships a complete starter package at ","type":"text"},{"code":"Templates\/NewGame","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — copy it out, rename it, and skim this guide for the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" behind each piece.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-Gnusto-to-your-package","text":"Add Gnusto to your package"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add Gnusto as a dependency, list it in your executable target, and give the test target the ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoTestSupport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product (it links the toolchain’s Testing library, so it belongs in test targets only):","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ swift-tools-version: 6.2","import PackageDescription","","let package = Package(","    name: \"MyGame\",","    platforms: [.macOS(.v15)],","    dependencies: [","        .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/Gnusto\", from: \"0.1.0\")","    ],","    targets: [","        .executableTarget(","            name: \"MyGame\",","            dependencies: [","                .product(name: \"Gnusto\", package: \"Gnusto\")","            ]","        ),","        .testTarget(","            name: \"MyGameTests\",","            dependencies: [","                \"MyGame\",","                .product(name: \"GnustoTestSupport\", package: \"Gnusto\"),","            ]","        ),","    ]",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gnusto requires macOS 15 or newer (it uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Synchronization.Mutex"},{"type":"text","text":"), and builds with the Swift 6 language mode."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Declare-a-game","text":"Declare a game"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A game is a single type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Start with just a title and an intro:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","","struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"type":"text","text":" requires an "},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", but Swift synthesizes it for free as long as every stored property has a default value — which they always will here, since rooms, items, and state are declared with initializers."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Add a room","anchor":"Add-a-room","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as a stored property. The property name ("},{"code":"hall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") becomes the room’s internal identity; the "},{"code":"name(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" trait is what the player sees."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","","    let hall = Location {","        name(\"Entrance Hall\")","        description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","    }","","    var map: WorldMap {","        player.starts(in: hall)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block is where geography and starting positions live. "},{"code":"player.starts(in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" places the player; without it, the game has nowhere to begin."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Run it","anchor":"Run-it","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three lines turn a game value into a running session:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld"},{"text":" validates the game and builds its initial state up front — a mistake like an exit to an undeclared room is caught here, as a thrown ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapError"},{"text":", not at runtime. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL"},{"text":" runs the prompt\/parse\/perform\/print loop, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ConsoleIOHandler"},{"text":" reads from and writes to the terminal.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wrap it in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"do","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"catch"},{"type":"text","text":" in your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"main.swift"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","","do {","    let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","    await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()","} catch {","    print(\"Couldn't start the game: \\(error)\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Run "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift run"},{"type":"text","text":", and you can already "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"look"},{"type":"text","text":" around and try to move."}]},{"anchor":"Add-a-second-room-and-connect-them","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Add a second room and connect them"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Exits are declared on locations in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block. Each directional method (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/north(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)"},{"text":", …) is an ordinary property reference, so a typo or a renamed room is a compile error, not a broken game.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let hall = Location {","    name(\"Entrance Hall\")","    description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","}","","let library = Location {","    name(\"Dusty Library\")","    description(\"Shelves sag under mildewed books. The hall lies south.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are one-directional by design — declare both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hall.north(library)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"library.south(hall)"},{"type":"text","text":" if you want the player to be able to walk back."}]},{"anchor":"Add-a-thing","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Add a thing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" the same way, then place it in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let lantern = Item {","    name(\"brass lantern\")","    adjectives(\"brass\", \"old\")","    description(\"An old brass lantern, its glass sooty but intact.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","    lantern.starts(in: library)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the player can walk "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"north"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"examine lantern"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take lantern"},{"type":"text","text":", and see it in their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inventory"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" let them type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take brass lantern"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take old lantern"},{"type":"text","text":"; a phrase has to end on a noun, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take brass"},{"type":"text","text":" on its own is not one of them. The last word of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (“lantern”) is the noun the parser keys on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything you declare is split into words the same way the parser splits what the player types — lowercased, a trailing possessive dropped, every other punctuation mark a separator. So "},{"code":"name(\"Mrs. Vane\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" prints its period and answers to "},{"code":"mrs vane","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"adjectives(\"master's\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same declaration as "},{"code":"adjectives(\"master\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Write the second: a declaration should read the way the parser stores it."}]},{"text":"React with a rule","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"React-with-a-rule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So far every verb uses its built-in behavior. To add your own logic, write a rule in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block. Rules are ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"after","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hooks attached to a location, an item, or the whole world.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var rules: Rules {","    lantern.after(.take) {","        say(\"It's heavier than it looks.\")","    }","","    library.before(.go) {","        guard command.direction != .south else { return }","        try refuse(\"There's no exit that way — only back south to the hall.\")","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first rule runs "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the player successfully takes the lantern and adds a line of flavor with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The second runs "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" movement in the library and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"s any direction but south. Inside a rule body, bare identifiers like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"command"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player"},{"type":"text","text":", and your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lantern"},{"type":"text","text":" refer to the live turn — reading and writing them touches the current game state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To learn what rules can do — the phases, the ordering, and the difference between "},{"code":"refuse","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"reply","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"say","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"end","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — read "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Test-it","text":"Test it","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A play session is just typed input and printed output, so the natural test plays a scripted session and asserts on the transcript:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","struct MyGameTests {","    @Test func theLanternIsWhereTheBreezeSaysItIs() async throws {","        let transcript = try await play(MyGame(), [\"north\", \"take lantern\"])","        expectInOrder(transcript, [\"Dusty Library\", \"Taken.\"])","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"play","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" boots the game and feeds it each command; ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectInOrder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" asserts the beats appear in order and shows the full transcript when one doesn’t. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for turn slicing and pinning the random stream.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-fuller-example","type":"heading","text":"A fuller example","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Gnusto ships with ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cloak of Darkness","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", Roger Firth’s classic one-room demonstration game, as its ","type":"text"},{"code":"CloakOfDarkness","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" target. It exercises nearly every feature in a page of code — dark rooms, a wearable cloak, scored actions, a losing state, and per-turn rules — and is worth reading start to finish once the basics click.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Next-steps","type":"heading","text":"Next steps","level":2},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Templates\/NewGame"},{"type":"text","text":" in the repo — the complete starter package this guide builds up to"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — how declarations, identity, and live references fit together","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true},{"text":" — exactly what happens each turn","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — the full vocabulary of game logic"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","type":"reference"},{"text":" — teach the parser new words with ","type":"text"},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame"},{"type":"text","text":" — transcript tests with GnustoTestSupport"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — carry your own data on entities and in globals","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/gettingstarted"]}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location/south(_:)":{"title":"south(_:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"An exit leading south to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"to"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location\/south(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"south"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Location"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"text":"MapEntry","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8MapEntryV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/CustomStateAndTraits":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Carry your own data on entities and in globals, alongside the engine’s closed core."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/customstateandtraits","title":"Custom State and Traits","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/refuse(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/refuse(_:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Blocks the current action with a complaint. The default action and any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remaining ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"after","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rules are skipped; world time still passes.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"refuse(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refuse","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Never","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TheTurnPipeline":{"abstract":[{"text":"What happens between the player pressing Return and the next prompt.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"The Turn Pipeline","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/theturnpipeline"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/AddingCustomVerbs":{"abstract":[{"text":"Teach the parser words the built-in table doesn’t know.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Adding Custom Verbs","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/addingcustomverbs"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location/north(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location\/north(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/north(_:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An exit leading north to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"to"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"north(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"north"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Location"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MapEntry","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8MapEntryV"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WritingRules":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach game logic to items, locations, and the world."}],"title":"Writing Rules","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/writingrules"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A place in the world.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Location","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TestingYourGame":{"abstract":[{"text":"Play scripted sessions in your test suite and assert on the transcript.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/testingyourgame","type":"topic","title":"Testing Your Game"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","title":"Gnusto","abstract":[{"text":"A Swift engine for writing parser-driven interactive fiction — text adventures in the tradition of Zork and Infocom’s ZIL.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/BootstrapError":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/bootstraperror","type":"topic","title":"BootstrapError","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BootstrapError","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BootstrapError","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapError","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"All problems with a game definition, reported at once."}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/REPL":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/repl","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The outer loop: prompt → parse → perform → print, until the game ends or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input runs out. Holds the only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" in a Gnusto game."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"REPL","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"REPL","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"REPL","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item":{"title":"Item","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","abstract":[{"text":"A thing in the world.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/say(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/say(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Prints a message as part of the turn’s output.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"say(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"say"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/adjectives(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Additional words the parser accepts before the item’s noun."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"adjectives(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"adjectives","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"...) -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9ItemTraitV","text":"ItemTrait"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ConsoleIOHandler":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConsoleIOHandler"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConsoleIOHandler","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ConsoleIOHandler","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain terminal IO."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/consoleiohandler","type":"topic","title":"ConsoleIOHandler","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameWorld":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GameWorld","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameWorld","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The game world: owns all state, serializes all mutation, and runs the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"turn pipeline. The single "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" in a game sits between the REPL and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this actor."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gameworld","title":"GameWorld","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/AnatomyOfAGame":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/anatomyofagame","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"How a single Swift type becomes a world the engine can run.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Anatomy of a Game"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Game":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A complete game: declarations, geography, and rules.","type":"text"}],"title":"Game","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/game","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"}}}